    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai, mini.surround\n\n### Description\n\nI am a long time [treesitter-textobjects](https://github.com/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter-textobjects/) user but recently I decided to give `mini.ai` a try because being able to choose `search_method` is a very powerful feature.\n\nUsing regex textobjects for selecting Markdown emphasis is not ideal because it treats everything in between two emphasis as an emphasis in it self (see similar  #1223). That is why I would like to use TreeSitter with custom queries for defining such textobjects.\n\nCode block textobject example\n\nHere is `after/queries/markdown/textobjects.scm`:\n\n``` Scheme\n; extends\n\n(fenced_code_block\n  (code_fence_content) @cell.inner) @cell.outer\n```\n\nAnd setup:\n\n``` lua\nd = spec_treesitter({ a = '@cell.outer', i = '@cell.inner' }),\n```\n\nIt works as expected. The problem is that `emphasis`, `strong_emphasis` and many other elements are defined inside `markdown_inline` parser instead of `markdown`. \n\nHere is `after/queries/markdown_inline/textobjects.scm`:\n\n``` Scheme\n; extends\n\n(emphasis) @emphasis.outer\n((emphasis) @emphasis.inner\n    (#offset! @emphasis.inner 0 1 0 -1))\n```\n\nAnd plugin setup:\n\n``` lua\ni = spec_treesitter({ a = '@emphasis.outer', i = '@emphasis.inner' }),\n```\n\nWhile code block textobject (`d`) works perfectly fine, emphasis textobject (`i`) does not work at all, it does not even throw errors on invalid query file inside `markdown_inline/`.\n\nDocumentation for `MiniAi.gen_spec.treesitter()` [says](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/be81509b7160aa02264a59789164a2e1c4a6750a/doc/mini-ai.txt#L775):\n> it uses buffer's |filetype| to determine query language.\n\nWhat I suppose is happening is that it look for textobjects inside `<vim.bo.filetype>/textobjects.scm` which is `markdown/textobjects.scm` and it does not search `markdown_inline/textobjects.scm` at all.\n\nI would expect Markdown files to be a special case that triggers reading `markdown_inline` query files as well because this is what [treesitter-textobjects](https://github.com/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter-textobjects/) I suppose is doing. `:=require(\"nvim-treesitter-textobjects.select\").select_textobject(\"@emphasis.outer\", \"textobjects\")` works as expected while `vani` does not.\n\nI even tried enabling `use_nvim_treesitter` like this:\n\n``` lua\ni = spec_treesitter({ a = '@emphasis.outer', i = '@emphasis.inner' }, { use_nvim_treesitter = true })\n```\n\nBut it didn't help",
