            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\n> While code block textobject (`d`) works perfectly fine, emphasis textobject (`i`) does not work at all, it does not even throw errors on invalid query file inside `markdown_inline/`.\n\nCould you please provide a concrete steps to reproduce this? Like:\n- All queries that are added to the setup.\n- The exact setup of `require('mini.ai').setup()` and/or `require('mini.surround').setup()`.\n- Example of a markdown file, cursor position, and keys with which to reproduce the issue.\n\nAll of the above ideally should be reproducible in the clean config (like with using `NVIM_APPNAME=nvim-repro`; more steps are described in the issue template for the \"Bug\" issue).\n\nAt the moment the general direction of the issue is clear, but there is nothing obviously wrong with either 'mini.ai' / 'mini.surround' code or the assumed setup. So the details are important here.",
