            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I was able to reproduce the described behavior with configuration as minimal as this:\n\n``` lua\n-- init.lua\nlocal ai = require(\"mini.ai\")\nai.setup({\n    custom_textobjects = {\n        i = ai.gen_spec.treesitter({ a = '@emphasis.outer', i = '@emphasis.inner' }),\n        d = ai.gen_spec.treesitter({ a = '@cell.outer', i = '@cell.inner' }),\n    },\n})\n```\n\nQuery file located at `after/queries/markdown_inline/textobjects.scm`:\n\n``` Scheme\n; extends\n\n(emphasis) @emphasis.outer\n((emphasis) @emphasis.inner\n    (#offset! @emphasis.inner 0 1 0 -1))\n```\n\nQuery file located at `after/queries/markdown/textobjects.scm`:\n\n``` Scheme\n; extends\n\n(fenced_code_block\n  (code_fence_content) @cell.inner) @cell.outer\n```\n\nExample markdown file (replaced \\`\\`\\` wiht \\\\\\`\\`\\` for better readability on GitHub):\n\n```` markdown\n## Header\n\nSome text, *some* more text\n\n``` lua\nlocal a = 'hello'\n```\n\nSome test\n````\n\nAnd 'mini.ai' being the only plugin installed (installed by NixOS, not plugin manager; never had an issue because of that)\n\nWith this setup and cursor being on line `1` and column `1` pressing `vid` selects the insides of code block and pressing `vii` just prints `(nini.ai) No textobject \"ii\" found covering region within 50 lines and ~search_method = 'cover_or_next'`. ",
