            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> could you please double check if all of this makes sense?\n\nYeah, that seems to be the exact cause of the issue.\n\nSince `markdown`/`markdown_inline` are a really particular case of treesitter parser/injections, a possible solution while keeping #2009 approach could be to special case `markdown` to check first level children `lang_tree`s where `lang == 'markdown_inline'` for textobjects. Treating both as part of the same \"language\". This could have the possible benefit of providing a general approach if it would be needed to handle something similar for other languages. But, I don't think this particular edge case would be common in other languages/tree-sitter parsers.",
