            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Since `markdown`/`markdown_inline` are a really particular case of treesitter parser/injections, a possible solution while keeping [#2009](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/pull/2009) approach could be to special case `markdown` to check first level children `lang_tree`s where `lang == 'markdown_inline'` for textobjects. Treating both as part of the same \"language\".\n\nI really, **really** would like to avoid doing language specific exceptions in 'mini.nvim' as much as possible.\n\nIs there any way to solve this on a tree-sitter level? Like some query magic, maybe?",
