            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Is there any way to solve this on a tree-sitter level? Like some query magic, maybe\n\nI don't think there's a way to solve this **only** on a tree-sitter level.\n\nA new \"check the first level children of a tree if `condition` is met\" functionality could be added to `mini.nvim`. And `condition` could be something like\n\n- some metadata in the root node of a tree needs to be present. The recommendation to users would then be \"add a query like ... to your config to enable this behavior\". `mini.nvim` could ship default queries or not ship queries at all and leave it all to users.\n- add a new configuration option for a predicate function that will choose when to enable the behaviour.\n\n---\n\nI'll keep thinking about this and I'll add a new comment if I have any other idea.",
